{"kind":"propose","text":"Review note for Hugh: keep corrections on the commitment that already owes them.\n\nRecommendation: clarify the agent instructions so a review finding that only identifies an unmet existing condition normally stays on the same implementation request and promise. Publish the corrected exact-head artifact and obtain fresh independent review as usual. Create a child assignment when the finding creates a separate outcome, changes the conditions or authority, or assigns work to another performer. Keep explicit successor transfer for an actual replacement assignment.\n\nThe reason is visible in my own coordination tonight. After genuine findings on I1 head 605163a3 and UI-plan head 65097650, I filed repair children 537c93fe and 07e8e481. Claude promised both, and I superseded their predecessors through ee384f85 and 7fbf0f25. That is six assignment/claim/transfer events across two correction rounds, in addition to the necessary review verdicts and ratifications. Inspection now shows both predecessor commitments superseded and both successor chains stale through those retirements. I then had to explain that conditions, availability and decisions remained current. These transfers preserve the work correctly under the route I chose; they do not demonstrate that replacement tasks were needed to repair the original promised result.\n\nThe instructions invite different readings. At current main 3f4c4969, AGENTS.md says 'If work is discovered mid-flight, create a child request ... before implementing it'; SKILL.md discipline 9 likewise asks for a child when repair work is needed. But SKILL.md's review rule says a changes-requested verdict does not close the implementation commitment, and describes a transfer conditionally: 'When the requester moves the required repair into a child request'. The existing work-loop page reserves promotion for changed scope, changed conditions or follow-up work. The ambiguity is whether fixing an already-promised condition is a newly assigned task.\n\nThere is a concrete simpler history. Tailapp Stage 2 request #2977, promise #2980, received changes-requested verdicts #2994 and #3009 for its README installation sequence. Corrected artifacts remained on that same promise; fresh review requests #3007 and #3022 led to approval #3024 at e3f71d42. The commitment is satisfied in the inspected snapshot. The second review correctly discovered that the first suggested fix was incomplete. The useful safety work was retained without inserting a replacement implementation request between these reviews. Canonical evidence is attached; this is a single worked example, not a claim that every historical repair used this shape.\n\nSuggested instruction:\n'Corrections needed to satisfy an existing request remain on its live commitment when the outcome, conditions, performer, destination and governing authority are unchanged. Cite the review finding in the corrected artifact, publish the new exact head and request fresh independent review. File a child request before work that adds a separate outcome, changes those conditions or authority, or needs a different performer. Transfer the original commitment only when responsibility for its remaining outcome actually moves.'\n\nThis would leave the fold, signatures, independent review, exact-head approval, explicit review ratification and sealed delivery unchanged. A changed destination or hold owner still needs the existing explicit authority and replacement procedure. Separate repair work and material scope changes remain durably assigned. The current two repair transfers should finish through their already-promised successors, not be undone for tidiness.\n\nRequested decision: approve a bounded clarification of the instructions and a trial on the next five qualifying correction rounds. Check that every finding remains traceable to a corrected artifact and independent verdict, the original commitment stays visible until delivery, and scope/authority changes still receive a new assignment. Count avoided replacement requests and continuity explanations; record review defects separately and make no time-saving claim without effort evidence. This complements the adopted review-binding preparation work; it does not expand that implementation request. No instruction or runtime change is adopted by this review note.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c3e8bca80c7eaf32d38916c72c3cfb0b45703135 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:05620034d53d513c4df269914dd03114d8b784d4, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:153178f947c18549b30814a5a23689b90de05349, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2ad49e23fb2bba11b4ebdd92ed15a676a4c9fca0, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:47da5df440351df81e01e035f951c8ee6d757554 and 10 more"}}